a 43:27 ׳ ר absolute, first of mankind Job 15:17 absolute of ׳ י , I (an the) first Isa 41:4 (+ אֶתֿ אַחֲדֹנִים ), + אַחְרוֺן Isa 44:6 ; Isa 48:12 absolute of time, מֵרִאשׁוֺן Jer 17:12 from the beginning ; especially first of a def. series (sometimes opposed to אַחֲרוֺן ). first day of feast Deut 16:4 ; Exod 12:15 (twice in verse); Exod 12:16 + 5 t. P ( H ), Neh 8:18 , usually first month ( חֹרֶשׁ ) Exod 40:2 ; Exod 40:17 ; Lev 23:5 + 6 t. P , 1Chr 12:16 ( van d. H. v. 1Chr 12:15 ) + 10 t. Chronicles, Ezra, Esth 3:7 ; Dan 10:4 , חֹדֶשׁ omitted Gen 8:13 ; Exod 12:2 ; Exod 12:18 ; Num 9:5 (all P ) Ezek 29:17 ; Ezek 30:20 ; Ezek 45:18 ; Ezek 45:21 , so Joel 2:23 , but read כָּרִאשׁוֺנָה ( 3 a ) ᵐ5 ᵑ6 We Now and Dr . \\ \\ b. first in degree, chief: יַד הַשָּׂרִיםרִ֗֗֗אשׁוֺנָה Ezra 9:2 the hand of the princes ... has been first in this trespass; 1Chr 18:17 ; Dan 10:13 (Chronicles, Esth 1:14 below). 3. a. feminine with preposition as adverb phrase: (1) of time, בָּרִאשֹׁנָה Gen 13:4 ( J ), = before, formerly , so Josh 8:5 ; Josh 8:6 ( J E ), 2Sam 7:10 ; 2Sam 20:18 ; Jer 7:12 ; Isa 52:4 , ׳ לָר = before, formerly , Gen 28:19 ( J ), Judg 18:29 so ׳ כְּבָר as formerly Judg 20:32 ; 1Kgs 13:6 ; Isa 1:26 ; Jer 33:7 ; Jer 33:11 , = ׳ כָּ ר Deut 9:15 ; Dan 11:29 (opposed to כָּאַחֲרוֺנָה ); בָּר = at first , first of all, Deut 13:10 ; Deut 17:7 ; ( P ) Josh 8:33 ( D ), 1Kgs 17:13 ; 1Kgs 20:9 ; Zech 12:7 ; Prov 20:21 (opposed to אַחֲרִיתָהּ ), 1Chr 11:6 (twice in verse); 1Chr 17:9 ; Neh 7:5 לְמַבָּרִאשׁוֺנָה 1Chr 15:13 (= ׳ לְמַהבָּֿר ) for what was at first , etc. ( מָךְ 1 e ); (2) location, ׳ בָּר i.e. at the head of an army 1Kgs 20:17 , a procession Num 10:14 ( P ), compare Isa 60:9 . \\ \\ b. רִאשֹׁנָה alone as adverb: (1) of time first Gen 38:28 ( J ), 1Kgs 18:25 ; Jer 16:18 ; Lev 5:8 ; Num 2:9 ; Josh 21:10 (all P ), Isa 65:7 ( Ew De Che Di Du Skinner, >adjective Ges Hi Kn ); (2) of place Gen 33:2 ( J ); (3) of degree, rank, Esth 1:14 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry oncl